1
00:00:26,670 --> 00:00:33,929
Our 9-service test shop, live: traces, metrics and logs flow through OpenTelemetry, Jaeger and Prometheus.

2
00:00:33,929 --> 00:00:39,588
We inject a known fault into our own test environment: a bad deployment of the payment service.

3
00:00:39,588 --> 00:00:45,698
Within a minute, errors spread upstream: checkout and frontend turn red too. Which service is the real cause?

4
00:00:45,698 --> 00:00:47,323
The on-call engineer pastes the alert and clicks Investigate.

5
00:00:47,323 --> 00:00:56,323
EvidenceTrail scans health, walks the call graph, prefetches evidence, then Gemini tests hypotheses with read-only tools.

6
00:01:09,766 --> 00:01:17,147
Diagnosis: payment, caused by a bad deploy, with confidence, time, tokens and evidence precision.

7
00:01:17,147 --> 00:01:23,656
The blast radius shows the failure path, and the timeline shows exactly where the seconds went.

8
00:01:23,656 --> 00:01:29,420
Every claim links to the evidence behind it. Claims citing evidence that was never fetched are blocked.

9
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:36,238
Click any citation to see the exact log line, trace or deploy event, redacted before it reaches Gemini.

10
00:01:36,238 --> 00:01:45,238
The suggested fix is labelled by policy, shown as a dry run, and runs only with a named human approval.

11
00:01:46,156 --> 00:01:51,291
After approval the deploy is rolled back and the services recover.

12
00:01:51,291 --> 00:02:00,291
Measured on injected faults, misses included: EvidenceTrail vs single-prompt Gemini vs a dashboard rule.

